Specification repository. It holds the AIP specification, its Internet-Draft renderings, JSON schemas, generated registries, and Python check scripts with their regression tests. It has no CLI, package, build, or published artifact, so the CLI phases of the 8-phase /pre-push-review (new-user walkthrough, adversarial corpus, score sanity, concept-explainer, real-world dev-tree scan) are not applicable. Before a push, run the tests and checks from the repository root: python3 -m unittest discover -s tests; python3 scripts/test_checks.py; python3 scripts/validate_examples.py (needs the jsonschema package); python3 scripts/gen_registries.py --check. CI runs the last two on every pull request and on pushes to main. Review of spec text happens via PR review and downstream issue threads.
